==Spanish==
{{wikipedia|lang=es}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|es}} {{m|la|calōre}}, singular ablative of {{m|la|calor||heat, warmth}}, ''calōrem''. Compare French {{m|fr|chaleur}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ka̠ˈlo̞ɾ]|lang=es}}
* {{rhymes|oɾ|lang=es}}

===Noun===
{{es-noun|m|es}}

# [[heat]]
#: ''Tengo '''calor'''.''
#:: ''I'm hot. (lit. I have '''heat''').''

====Antonyms====
* {{l|es|frío}}

====Usage notes====
* In northern Mexico, ''calor'' is colloquially feminine. Adjectives are affected as well. ''Hace mucha calor'' thus is equal to ''hace mucho calor''.

